{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4e7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c36e-d989-7603-9e05-f0fee9b1e516"},"sequence":206,"recorded_at":1780531400000407,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623"},"call_id":"call_01a0c36fa31476a2be2b13d7bef6c6b1","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(1219 line(s) above)\n1220|### 4.D Closed capabilities and evidence\n1221|\n1222|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapability</dfn> is the exact 16-value registry below.\n1223|<dfn>TerminalBackendOperation</dfn> is exactly\n1224|<code>manifest|probe|create|attach|status|quiesce-input|wait-safe-boundary|request-stop|terminate-stale|restore</code>.\n1225|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceRequirement</dfn> is exactly\n1226|<code>conformance_fixture|runtime_probe|credential_sentinel|provider_auth_smoke|policy_authorization</code>.\n1227|\n1228|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1229|<code>capability:TerminalBackendCapability</code>,\n1230|<code>origin:static|probed</code>, <code>value:boolean</code>,\n1231|<code>generation_variable:boolean</code>,\n1232|<code>dependent_operations:sorted-unique TerminalBackendOperation[1..10]</code>,\n1233|and <code>evidence_requirements:sorted-unique CapabilityEvidenceRequirement[1..5]</code>.\n1234|The latter three members MUST exactly equal the registry row for the capability;\n1235|a Manifest or Probe cannot redefine them. A false claim is retained to make a\n1236|probed refusal explicit but confers no operation.\n1237|\n1238|| Capability | Exact semantics | Generation-variable | Exact dependent operations | Exact evidence requirements |\n1239|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1240|| <code>durable_disconnect</code> | Wrapper survives every client disconnect. | false | <code>create,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1241|| <code>local_attach</code> | Local-only presentation. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1242|| <code>remote_attach</code> | Presentation over trusted private mesh only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1243|| <code>web_attach</code> | Web presentation over an admitted transport only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1244|| <code>multi_attach</code> | Concurrent presentation clients; no multi-input or ownership implication. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1245|| <code>headless_creation</code> | Create without UI or prompt in the proven execution realm. | true | <code>create</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1246|| <code>reboot_restoration</code> | Re-establish after reboot; does not claim process survival. | true | <code>restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1247|| <code>input_quiescence</code> | Reject new input with generation-bound evidence. | true | <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1248|| <code>safe_boundary_observation</code> | Observe AX/provider-selected safe-boundary proof. | true | <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1249|| <code>provider_process_observation</code> | Observe provider presence without PID identity. | true | <code>status,terminate-stale,wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1250|| <code>graceful_stop</code> | Request and observe orderly exit. | true | <code>request-stop</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1251|| <code>stale_process_termination</code> | Target one fenced stale incarnation. | true | <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1252|| <code>terminal_state_retention</code> | Retain local presentation state, never portable Checkpoint state. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1253|| <code>scrollback_retention</code> | Retain local scrollback, never replicated terminal output. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1254|| <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> | Exact instance passes AX sentinel and provider-auth smoke without UI. | true | <code>create,restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,credential_sentinel,provider_auth_smoke,runtime_probe</code> |\n1255|| <code>multiple_input_clients</code> | Backend serializes multiple input clients; AX policy separately authorizes use. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1256|\n1257|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceFact</dfn> is the exact enum\n1258|<code>fixture_passed|runtime_probe_passed|sentinel_passed|provider_auth_passed|policy_checked|ui_absent|prompt_absent</code>.\n1259|Capability Evidence 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no other\n1260|member is permitted:\n1261|\n1262|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1263|| --- | --- |\n1264|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-capability-evidence</code> |\n1265|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1266|| <code>evidence_id</code> | digest computed by the Section 4.B identity rule |\n1267|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1268|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to Manifest and Probe |\n1269|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver equal to Probe |\n1270|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest equal to Probe |\n1271|| <code>capability</code> | TerminalBackendCapability |\n1272|| <code>value</code> | literal <code>true</code> |\n1273|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> equal to Probe |\n1274|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] equal to Probe |\n1275|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest equal to Manifest |\n1276|| <code>observed_at</code> | timestamp |\n1277|| <code>expires_at</code> | timestamp strictly after <code>observed_at</code> |\n1278|| <code>issuer</code> | <code>ax_release|ax_local_probe</code> |\n1279|| <code>issuer_id</code> | digest of the AX release signing identity for <code>ax_release</code>, or digest of the host-incarnation identity for <code>ax_local_probe</code> |\n1280|| <code>attestation_signature</code> | <code>rsa-sha256:</code> plus Base64 RFC 4648 signature by the trusted <code>issuer_id</code> key over the domain-separated JCS object with <code>evidence_id</code> and this member omitted |\n1281|| <code>facts</code> | sorted unique CapabilityEvidenceFact[1..7] |\n1282|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1283|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1284|| <code>provider_build</code> | string[1..256]|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1285|| <code>sentinel_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1286|| <code>provider_auth_smoke_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1287|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1288|\n1289|Credential-realm evidence binds the opaque Terminal Instance Binding digest,\n1290|AX-owned sentinel result, provider ID/build, and provider-auth smoke result. It\n1291|contains neither the Terminal Instance ID nor raw generation.\n1292|The signed bytes are ASCII <code>ax-terminal-capability-evidence-v1</code>, one\n1293|zero byte, and the Section 1.6 canonical bytes of the evidence object after\n1294|omitting exactly <code>evidence_id</code> and <code>attestation_signature</code>.\n1295|AX resolves <code>issuer_id</code> through its trusted release/host-incarnation\n1296|key registry and MUST verify the signature before treating the object as\n1297|evidence; a caller-supplied issuer ID is not authentication. Missing, malformed,\n1298|unknown-key, or invalid signatures fail closed before capability admission.\n1299|GUI/Aqua bootstrap alone is not proof. Missing, expired, self-minted,\n1300|contradictory, or wrong-generation evidence disables the claim. Static claims\n1301|never override a failed probe; generation-variable claims re-probe on generation\n1302|change and before activation.\n1303|\n1304|Multi/remote/web attach never implies multiple authorized input sources or\n1305|ownership. Multi-input is separately declared and policy-gated. Restore/resume\n1306|MUST NOT silently fall back to another backend; defaults apply only to new\n1307|activation when policy allows.\n1308|\n1309|### 4.E Persistence, transport, security, and compatibility\n1310|\n1311|| Classification | Members and rule |\n1312|| --- | --- |\n1313|| Safe immutable evidence | Sanitized backend identity/version/platform/conformance/capability evidence; MAY persist and replicate after validation. |\n1314|| Host-local durable metadata | Instance/binding IDs, sanitized native reference, generation, idempotency receipt, last effect; host-local, non-replicable. |\n1315|| Derived cache | Discovery/availability/attachability/process observations and probe views; rebuildable, non-authoritative. |\n1316|| Sensitive runtime state | IPC, tmux sockets, named pipes, attach/relay credentials, backend auth/live databases, GUI/login attestations, provider credentials; owner-only and non-replicable. |\n1317|| Forbidden | Raw native reference, PID/handle, endpoint/token, terminal output/scrollback, unrestricted environment, credential detail, and live-process facts MUST NOT replicate. |\n1318|\n1319|Presentation transport is exactly <code>local_only</code>,\n1320|<code>trusted_private_mesh</code>, or <code>third_party_relay</code>. Current AX\n1321|admits only the first two. A relay-required/public-service backend is unavailable\n1322|pending explicit future product/contract approval. AX retains no permanent\n1323|public TCP listener. Attach transport carries no AX authoritative state,\n1324|provider store, workspace, Checkpoint, task-board data, or ownership change.\n1325|\n1326|The exact v0.4.3 Configuration 1/2 <code>tmux|conpty</code>, Provider Protocol 2\n1327|TerminalDescriptor, Session Event 1 terminal payloads, and CLI Result 1 start/\n1328|resume shapes and digests remain immutable. Version adapters deterministically\n1329|map legacy <code>tmux</code> to <code>ax.tmux</code> and <code>conpty</code> to\n1330|<code>ax.conpty</code>, with version/generation <code>legacy_unreported</code>\n1331|and no inferred capabilities. Reverse projection exists only for those two IDs;\n1332|other IDs return <code>incompatible_schema</code>, never fallback. Translation\n1333|never rewrites or re-digests history.\n1334|\n1335|New readers accept old objects through the adapter. Old readers may browse/sync\n1336|opaque newer immutable records but cannot activate, restore, or write them.\n1337|Mixed peers negotiate each containing contract independently; no common backend\n1338|major means browse/sync only. Unknown/unsupported IDs remain visible as unknown/\n1339|unavailable; registry read failure is never absence. Lower-version writers are\n1340|read-only and cannot write downgrade replacements. Bootstrap permits only a\n1341|framed <code>manifest</code> call in an understood major. Capability negotiation\n1342|is the intersection plus valid bound evidence, never union or inference.\n1343|\n1344|Mesh RPC 4.0.0 is defined normatively in Section 11.9: its exact 25-key hello\n1345|map changes the RPC and Session Event arrays and adds exactly\n1346|<code>terminal_backend_evidence=[\"1.0.0\"]</code>; its exact eighth namespace\n1347|contains only sanitized Manifest, Probe, and Capability Evidence objects.\n1348|Terminal Instance Binding remains host-local durable metadata and is not a\n1349|namespace member; replicated Session Events carry only its digest as an opaque\n1350|audit reference. RPC 2/3 peers report this namespace unsupported, never empty.\n1351|\n1352|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 and its exact TerminalDescriptor are defined in\n1353|Section 7.A. Session Event 4.0.0 and its exact\n1354|<code>terminal.created</code>/<code>session.resumed</code> payloads are defined\n1355|in Section 5.2; neither payload contains a Terminal Instance ID, backend\n1356|generation, or native reference. CLI Result 4.0.0 local inspection and\n1357|start/resume bodies are defined in Section 14.6. Structured Error 1.3.0 literal\n1358|codes, exit classes, and bootstrap behavior are defined in Section 15.3. These\n1359|canonical definitions, not this compatibility summary, determine their closed\n1360|shapes.\n1361|\n1362|**Future candidate (non-normative; unavailable): Superlogical.** Dated public\n1363|sources retrieved 2026-08-29 describe planned reconnect/share, web/native\n1364|clients, software-driven structured actions, and libghostty use; the official\n1365|GitHub organization exposed no public repositories that day. They establish no\n1366|public release, AX adapter, API/SDK/protocol, backend ID/version, capability\n1367|evidence, lifecycle, ownership, security, or replication contract. The label\n1368|enables nothing. Admission requires dated evidence for create, attach/reconnect,\n1369|status/generation, quiescence, graceful/stale stop, restore, exact\n1370|<code>ax pane</code>, headless automation, credential proof, transport/auth,\n1371|no AX ownership/authoritative-state transfer, and crash/security/conformance\n1372|negative tests.\n1373|\n1374|### 4.1 Terminal backend interface\n1375|\n1376|Every terminal backend MUST implement these semantic operations:\n1377|\n1378|| Operation | Required result |\n1379|| --- | --- |\n1380|| <code>create</code> | With <code>session_id</code> and caller-stable <code>bootstrap_operation_id</code>, create a durable pane/process whose only stable entry point is <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>. |\n1381|| <code>attach</code> | Connect an operator to the local terminal without changing ownership. |\n1382|| <code>status</code> | Report process presence, wrapper state, provider child state, and attachability. |\n1383|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | Stop new operator/provider input while retaining observation. |\n1384|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | Prove the adapter-specific safe boundary or time out. |\n1385|| <code>request-stop</code> | Ask the provider to exit through a version-tested graceful path. |\n1386|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | Terminate a process only for explicit force recovery after preserving diagnostics. |\n1387|| <code>restore</code> | Recreate the wrapper after reboot and consult current ownership before any provider resume. |\n1388|\n1389|The wrapper MUST validate configuration, load the logical session, synchronize\n1390|known lease records when possible, and compare the local fencing token before\n1391|launching a provider. It MUST park safely when ownership is remote, ambiguous,\n1392|or unverified.\n1393|\n1394|Terminal creation and the wrapper's first child start are idempotent on\n1395|<code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code>. The backend MUST durably bind\n1396|that pair before child creation. An identical retry returns or reattaches to\n1397|the one recorded wrapper/child; changing the operation for a session still in\n1398|the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. After a lost result,\n1399|<code>status</code> plus that binding MUST prove absence or identify the one\n1400|child before any start retry. This contract never persists or replicates a PID\n1401|as identity.\n1402|\n1403|### 4.2 tmux backend\n1404|\n1405|On macOS, Linux, and WSL2, the supported durable terminal backend is tmux. Every\n1406|managed pane MUST run:\n1407|\n1408|~~~shell\n1409|ax pane <logical-session-id>\n1410|~~~\n1411|\n1412|It MUST NOT run the raw provider command as the pane's stable command.\n1413|<code>tmux-resurrect</code> plus <code>tmux-continuum</code> MAY recreate local\n1414|tmux layout and invoke the wrapper after reboot. They MUST NOT be described or\n1415|used as cross-host migration.\n1416|\n1417|AX MUST use its dedicated <code>-S</code> server and MUST NOT discover or reuse\n1418|the operator's default tmux server by ambient socket name. On macOS, server\n1419|creation is credential-sensitive. A Background caller MUST NOT create a\n1420|credential-dependent tmux server. A background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon,\n1421|or restore worker MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and\n1422|its attested AX tmux server; if neither exists it MUST return\n1423|<code>capability_unavailable</code> with typed realm/readiness details and MUST\n1424|NOT fall back to direct server creation.\n1425|\n1426|<code>launchctl managername</code> is a diagnostic hint only. Conformance\n1427|requires a functional AX sentinel inside the exact tmux server plus a separate\n1428|provider-auth smoke using the selected provider. Evidence MUST bind the exact\n1429|tmux server generation, provider build, and macOS version. Aqua alone and\n1430|sentinel-only evidence are insufficient. Any provider flow requiring GUI\n1431|interaction, Keychain UI, a permission prompt, or other human action fails\n1432|closed until that interaction succeeds in the verified GUI realm.\n1433|\n1434|After restore, the wrapper MUST:\n1435|\n1436|1. read the latest locally known lease;\n1437|2. attempt a mesh lease refresh without blocking forever;\n1438|3. resume locally only if the local host has the winning lease and the required\n1439|   materialization is valid;\n1440|4. offer remote attach/takeover when another host owns the session in an\n1441|   interactive terminal; or\n1442|5. enter <code>parked</code> without launching the provider in all other cases.\n1443|\n1444|Logout or reboot invalidates unrenewed realm evidence. Without a verified GUI\n1445|realm, recovery MUST remain parked until GUI login re-establishes the broker,\n1446|functional sentinel, provider-auth smoke, and their generation/build/version\n1447|binding. A cached sentinel or prior <code>managername</code> observation MUST\n1448|NOT authorize resume.\n1449|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
