{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6a3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c36e-d989-7603-9e05-f0fee9b1e516"},"sequence":428,"recorded_at":1780531400000851,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c370-9e9c-7ff2-952e-7d091dd32063"},"task_id":"01a0c370-9e9c-7ff2-952e-7d091dd32063","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c370-9e9c-7ff2-952e-7d091dd32063","chunk":"Read text file `internal/termbind/doc.go`.\n1|// Package termbind writes versioned terminal binding events, recovers\n2|// lost create results by bootstrap operation ID, and refuses PID/endpoint\n3|// identity. It is the final leaf of the ax-pane-and-terminal-instance-binding\n4|// story.\n5|//\n6|// Normative scope: AX v0.7.0 Section 4.B (Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0\n7|// closed object and the identity rule), Section 5.2 Session Event 4.0.0\n8|// Terminal Instance events (terminal.created and session.resumed v4\n9|// payloads), Section 4.D (evidence binding), Section 7.A (Provider\n10|// Protocol 3 descriptor identity, cited landed), and Section 13.1\n11|// (bootstrap idempotency and lost-result recovery).\n12|//\n13|// Division of authority (composed, never forked): v4 payload construction\n14|// and lease-authorized emission come from internal/axpane\n15|// (TerminalCreatedPayload, ResumedPayload, Emit); the durable bootstrap\n16|// binding comes from internal/axpane (Store.Bind/Lookup/Status); status\n17|// observation comes from internal/terminstance (Engine.ExecuteStatus);\n18|// backend admission comes from internal/terminalbackend\n19|// (Registry.AdmitProbe, ParseManifest, ParseProbe, ParseEvidence,\n20|// AdmitProviderDescriptor, GenerationDigest); event durability comes from\n21|// internal/sessrepo (AppendEvent); the newest-checkpoint window and the\n22|// lifecycle fold come from internal/sessstate (Reduce); UUIDv7, digest,\n23|// and timestamp grammars come from internal/scalar; strict object frames\n24|// come from internal/environ (DecodeStrictObject); closed event shapes\n25|// come from internal/canonicaljson at the append boundary. What this\n26|// package owns is the composition the earlier leaves deliberately left\n27|// out: the Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 parser (no parser exists on\n28|// trunk), the coded terminal-instance identity gate and its operation-body\n29|// pre-scans, evidence-ID resolution to admitted Manifest/Probe/Evidence\n30|// bound to the event tuple, the v4 emission entries, lost-create recovery,\n31|// and the durable attach-client receipt store.\n32|//\n33|// Bounds: no `ax` CLI surface, no tmux/ConPTY process control, no provider\n34|// process, and no mesh transport live here. CLI Result 4.0.0 is registered\n35|// but unimplemented in internal/cliresult, so the Result 4 identity\n36|// surface is a stated bound pinned by a tripwire test, not a gate.\n37|// Signature verification is caller-supplied through\n38|// terminalbackend.SignatureVerifier. The bootstrap window bit is derived\n39|// by the caller from the sessstate fold's newest checkpoint (the axpane\n40|// precedent for caller-derived facts); recovery tests close the loop by\n41|// folding a real chain.\n42|package termbind","final_result":true}}}
