{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6a7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c36e-d989-7603-9e05-f0fee9b1e516"},"sequence":430,"recorded_at":1780531400000855,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c370-9e71-7553-800c-6963fa097f84"},"task_id":"01a0c370-9e71-7553-800c-6963fa097f84","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c370-9e71-7553-800c-6963fa097f84","chunk":"Read text file `internal/secprim/doc.go`.\n1|// Package secprim implements the AX shared safe process and filesystem\n2|// primitives of pinned specification Sections 16.3, 16.4, and 16.7: no-follow\n3|// path handling, staging containment, structured argv, environment\n4|// allowlists, terminal control-string escaping, and secret redaction for\n5|// free-text streams.\n6|//\n7|// The package is a library behind production launch and rendering paths,\n8|// not a second authority beside them:\n9|//\n10|//   - path grammars stay in internal/scalar: CheckMemberPath admits exactly\n11|//     the scalar relative-path grammar plus the Windows alternate-stream,\n12|//     trailing-dot/space, and reserved-device rules Section 16.3 names, and\n13|//     delegates every shared rule to scalar rather than retyping it;\n14|//   - byte-counted exec rules (Provider SpawnPlan argv and env literals,\n15|//     Section 5.1) stay in internal/provhost: that package validates the\n16|//     wire plan, while this package builds the launch environment and\n17|//     validates the argv vector at process start;\n18|//   - environment-name grammar is owned here and internal/provhost delegates\n19|//     to it, so the two packages cannot drift on what a name is;\n20|//   - Structured Error detail redaction stays in internal/axerror: that\n21|//     package refuses exact credential keys and causal leaks on the error\n22|//     wire, while this package scrubs free-text streams (stderr, logs,\n23|//     terminal rendering) where no key gate can see;\n24|//   - SSH argv admission stays in internal/config and the provider entry\n25|//     point rule (`ax pane SESSION_ID`) stays in internal/terminalbackend:\n26|//     both are closed vocabularies over their own domain, not instances of\n27|//     the generic argv rule here;\n28|//   - the five-variable AX_* path registry stays in internal/config and\n29|//     internal/localstore, which already implement AC-PATH-001.\n30|//\n31|// Trust for external executables is deliberately not implemented here.\n32|// internal/provider.trustCandidate and internal/terminalbackend.DigestFile\n33|// already establish trust with different fact sets because their\n34|// specifications differ: Section 7.1 requires the approving owner identity\n35|// beside the canonical path and digest for provider plugins, while the\n36|// Section 4.B trust tuple carries platform, adapter identity, manifest and\n37|// probe digests with no owner fact. A third path here would be another\n38|// copy, not convergence; the difference is contractual, not accidental.\n39|//\n40|// Every refusal is a plain *Error naming the kind, rule, and member:\n41|// facades keep their own refusal dialects, so this package names rules\n42|// instead of minting codes, following internal/environ.\n43|//\n44|// Stated bounds. This package mutates no durable state and keeps no cache:\n45|// Guard resolution is lexical, OpenNoFollowFile opens read-only, and every\n46|// other entry point is a pure function of its input. Crash and idempotency\n47|// handling therefore have no surface here: there is no journal to recover\n48|// and no second actor to collide with. Tombstone deletion scope (Section\n49|// 16.3 \"broad deletion from tombstones\") has no implementation in this\n50|// repository yet and is not modeled. The operator default for which\n51|// environment names a provider plugin inherits is product policy with no\n52|// in-repo provider implementation to derive needs from, so BuildEnv takes\n53|// the allowlist explicitly and ExecRunner inherits the parent environment\n54|// until the operator supplies one. Grapheme-width policing stops at the\n55|// enumerated invisible controls: full East-Asian/emoji width measurement\n56|// needs terminal width tables this package does not carry. Content-level\n57|// secret scrubbing is best-effort by specification (Section 16.2 claims no\n58|// reliable scrubbing), and Redact states exactly the three shapes it\n59|// decides.\n60|package secprim","final_result":true}}}
