{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c731","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c36e-d989-7603-9e05-f0fee9b1e516"},"sequence":499,"recorded_at":1780531400000993,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c370-c08a-7cc2-bd4e-8f3ac0b2fd1d"},"task_id":"01a0c370-c08a-7cc2-bd4e-8f3ac0b2fd1d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c370-c08a-7cc2-bd4e-8f3ac0b2fd1d","chunk":"Read text file `internal/secprim/nofollow.go`.\n(99 line(s) above)\n100|// stated check-then-open bound. The returned file is cleared of\n101|// O_NONBLOCK like OpenNoFollowFile. The caller owns closing both the\n102|// root handle and the returned file.\n103|//\n104|// The handle is bound to the guard root before descending:\n105|// guardRootMatches fstats the handle and compares device and inode\n106|// against a stat of guard.root, refusing a foreign directory handle\n107|// with \"guard root mismatch\". The check lives here in shared code so\n108|// both platforms answer the mismatch identically; past it, the unix\n109|// walk descends from the verified handle and the Windows walk from the\n110|// verified root path, which name the same directory.\n111|func (guard Guard) Open(root *os.File, member string) (*os.File, error) {\n112|\tif err := CheckMemberPath(guard.platform, member); err != nil {\n113|\t\treturn nil, err\n114|\t}\n115|\tif guard.checkManaged && !guard.managed[member] {\n116|\t\treturn nil, failPath(\"member unmanaged\", memberErrorTarget(member))\n117|\t}\n118|\tif root == nil {\n119|\t\treturn nil, failPath(\"guard root handle\", memberErrorTarget(member))\n120|\t}\n121|\tif info, err := root.Stat(); err != nil || info == nil || !info.IsDir() {\n122|\t\treturn nil, failPath(\"guard root handle\", memberErrorTarget(member))\n123|\t}\n124|\tif !guardRootMatches(root, guard.root) {\n125|\t\treturn nil, failPath(\"guard root mismatch\", memberErrorTarget(member))\n126|\t}\n127|\tsegments := strings.Split(member, \"/\")\n128|\tfile, err := openCommitRelative(root, guard.root, member, segments)\n129|\tif err != nil {\n130|\t\tif errors.Is(err, errCommitSymlink) {\n131|\t\t\treturn nil, failPath(\"member symlink escape\", memberErrorTarget(member))\n132|\t\t}\n133|\t\treturn nil, failPath(\"open failed\", memberErrorTarget(member)).WithCause(err)\n134|\t}\n135|\tinfo, err := statOpenedFile(file)\n136|\tif err != nil {\n137|\t\t_ = file.Close()\n138|\t\treturn nil, failPath(\"open stat failed\", memberErrorTarget(member)).WithCause(err)\n139|\t}\n140|\tif err := CheckRegularTarget(info); err != nil {\n141|\t\t_ = file.Close()\n142|\t\treturn nil, err\n143|\t}\n144|\t_ = clearNonblock(file)\n145|\treturn file, nil\n146|}\n147|\n148|// statOpenedFile stats an already-opened descriptor. It is a variable\n149|// only so seam-failure tests can force the stat-failure path through the\n150|// production openers below: fstat on a live descriptor does not fail on\n151|// any supported platform, and without the seam the error branch is\n152|// untestable. Production code never reassigns it.\n153|var statOpenedFile = func(file *os.File) (os.FileInfo, error) {\n154|\treturn file.Stat()\n155|}\n156|\n157|// OpenNoFollowDir opens an existing directory read-only without following\n158|// a trailing symlink, returning a handle for validation walks. The handle\n159|// pins the opened directory: Fstat and ReadDirnames on it observe the\n160|// directory that was opened even if its name is later retargeted.\n161|//\n162|// The Lstat fast path refuses non-directories with the same rules on\n163|// every platform; the post-open Stat below stays authoritative against a\n164|// swap between the check and the open.\n165|func OpenNoFollowDir(path string) (*os.File, error) {\n166|\tif info, err := os.Lstat(path); err != nil {\n167|\t\treturn nil, failPath(\"open failed\", memberErrorTarget(path)).WithCause(err)\n168|\t} else if info.Mode()&os.ModeSymlink != 0 {\n169|\t\treturn nil, failPath(\"target symlink\", info.Name())\n170|\t} else if !info.IsDir() {\n171|\t\treturn nil, failPath(\"target directory\", info.Name())\n172|\t}\n173|\tdir, err := openNoFollowDir(path)\n174|\tif err != nil {\n175|\t\treturn nil, failPath(\"open failed\", memberErrorTarget(path)).WithCause(err)\n176|\t}\n177|\tinfo, err := statOpenedFile(dir)\n178|\tif err != nil {\n179|\t\t_ = dir.Close()\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
