{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c735","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c36e-d989-7603-9e05-f0fee9b1e516"},"sequence":501,"recorded_at":1780531400000997,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c370-c0a7-70c2-bf58-a9537a0fd387"},"task_id":"01a0c370-c0a7-70c2-bf58-a9537a0fd387","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c370-c0a7-70c2-bf58-a9537a0fd387","chunk":"Read text file `internal/termbind/identity.go`.\n1|package termbind\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"bytes\"\n5|\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n6|\t\"encoding/hex\"\n7|\t\"encoding/json\"\n8|\t\"strings\"\n9|\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n10|\n11|\t\"github.com/gowebpki/jcs\"\n12|\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/environ\"\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n15|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n16|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminstance\"\n17|)\n18|\n19|// BindingSchema is the Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 schema URN from\n20|// Section 4.B.\n21|const BindingSchema = \"urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding\"\n22|\n23|// BindingSchemaVersion is the only admitted binding schema version.\n24|const BindingSchemaVersion = \"1.0.0\"\n25|\n26|// CheckInstanceIdentity admits exactly the AX-allocated terminal instance\n27|// identity: a UUIDv7. A PID, handle, socket, path, named pipe, URL, token,\n28|// mutable endpoint, or native reference cannot spell a 36-character\n29|// hyphenated UUIDv7, so grammar admission is identity-shape admission (the\n30|// landed descriptor rationale, applied here as the story-level gate). Any\n31|// other value refuses terminal_backend_protocol_error: AX-local parsing of\n32|// a syntactically invalid identity, per the Section 4.C row note.\n33|func CheckInstanceIdentity(value string) error {\n34|\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(value); err != nil {\n35|\t\treturn &terminalbackend.Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"terminal instance identity\"}\n36|\t}\n37|\treturn nil\n38|}\n39|\n40|// Binding is the parsed Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 closed object: the\n41|// host-local durable metadata Section 4.B defines. It is never replicated;\n42|// replicated Session Events carry only its digest as an opaque audit\n43|// reference.\n44|type Binding struct {\n45|\tBindingID             string\n46|\tSessionID             string\n47|\tHostID                string\n48|\tHostIncarnationID     string\n49|\tTerminalInstanceID    string\n50|\tTerminalBackendID     string\n51|\tImplementationVersion string\n52|\tProtocolVersion       string\n53|\tBackendGeneration     string\n54|\tNativeReference       string\n55|\tCreatedAt             string\n56|\tSupersedesBindingID   string\n57|\tHasSupersedes         bool\n58|}\n59|\n60|// bindingMembers is the exact closed member set of the binding document,\n61|// in the order Section 4.B lists it.\n62|var bindingMembers = []string{\n63|\t\"schema\",\n64|\t\"schema_version\",\n65|\t\"binding_id\",\n66|\t\"session_id\",\n67|\t\"host_id\",\n68|\t\"host_incarnation_id\",\n69|\t\"terminal_instance_id\",\n70|\t\"terminal_backend_id\",\n71|\t\"implementation_version\",\n72|\t\"protocol_version\",\n73|\t\"backend_generation\",\n74|\t\"native_reference\",\n75|\t\"created_at\",\n76|\t\"supersedes_binding_id\",\n77|\t\"extensions\",\n78|}\n79|\n80|// ParseTerminalBinding admits one closed Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0\n81|// document. No parser exists on trunk for this schema, so this entry owns\n82|// it; every grammar delegates to its landed owner (frame to environ,\n83|// UUIDv7/digest/timestamp to scalar, backend ID and generation to\n84|// terminalbackend, semver to environ). The protocol_version member must\n85|// additionally select Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 and the\n86|// extensions member must be exactly the empty object {}, per the Section\n87|// 4.B table. The terminal_instance_id member passes through the coded\n88|// identity gate: a forbidden identity form refuses\n89|// terminal_backend_protocol_error. The binding_id member is recomputed by\n90|// the Section 4.B identity rule (digest of the RFC 8785 JCS bytes with the\n91|// ID member omitted, numbers and nested duplicates refused before the\n92|// transform) and must equal the carried value; a reader recompute\n93|// mismatch refuses terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch. Member-type\n94|// faults refuse the same protocol class as the landed descriptor parser:\n95|// a mistyped binding member is a malformed local document.\n96|func ParseTerminalBinding(raw []byte) (Binding, error) {\n97|\tempty := Binding{}\n98|\tmembers, fault := environ.DecodeStrictObject(raw)\n99|\tif fault != nil {\n100|\t\treturn empty, protocolRefusal(\"binding frame\")\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
