er` verdict (direction/tuple arms over a verified well-formed winner, no grant precondition — a grant authorizes, it never decides staleness) and composes it in `ObserveFencing` for grant-gated refusals, so the no-grant, lapsed-grant, no-clock and unusable-policy members fence from active/parked/quiescing under local and remote winners while unverified/ambiguous/winnerless/malformed/handoff-failed stay no-transition with the gate's own refusal or park; E3 commits the auth-expiry recheck witness (mid-operation expiry caught after one committed effect) plus a harness row that keeps the tuple recheck and drops the expiry recheck, and re-keys both E1 expired members onto the late-deadline instant so they kill on the receipt; P3-1..P3-4 commit the four reviewer witnesses with mirror rows, and P3-5 states the interim-proven create member with its `unavailable → terminate-stale` exit route.\n49|- F1: the grant-precondition class is exactly four members (no grant, no clock reading, lapsed grant, unusable policy) because those are all four refusals `Authorize` can surface after the ownership arms pass — the verdict decides the tuple fact for all four uniformly by never consulting grant/clock/policy, so completeness is structural, not enumerated, and the relative question needs no fallback (same grant facts, and the grant arms do not read `LocalHostID`).\n50|- F2: a narrowing row that spans a definition and its use is one plant, not two — the E3 row captures the entry instant and passes it to the in-loop authorization check, and either half alone breaks the build, so the kill measures the pair (same precedent as the rev3 resumption row spanning two adjacent checks).\n51|- F3: a grammar arm masked by a downstream arm is unmeasurable alone — the verdict's presented-session grammar arm needed the agreed-malformed member (both sides naming one malformed session, so only the grammar arm undecides it) because any other malformed session mismatches first.\n52|- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 114 narrowing mutants plus one tightening edge row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 116/116 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical before/after/across. The eleven verdict rows mutate the landed package and are killed through `ObserveFencing`, so the composition — not the helper — is measured. The five surviving rev3 reviewer narrowings (RV3-M1/M2/M3/M4/M8) are mirrored as committed rows with committed killers; RV3-M6/M7 were already killed by the committed suite. Retired `N-fencing-epoch-only` (provably equivalent post-fix: a stale park implies a decided-stale verdict and both arms call `fenceLive` with the same refusal) and re-keyed `N-fencing-operation` to the non-live killer (launch-class now shows on the surfaced park vocabulary). No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\n53|- AC: 93 of 93 rows driven through production entries by named tests (rows 1–84 keep rev3 numbers; rows 85–93 are the rework rows; matrix in `internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence carried from rev3 (no new durable write — the verdict and the recheck are pure over their inputs). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n54|\n55|### TASK-260830-kkh1an rev3 — Terminal Instance rework: resumption, remote fencing, row gates\n56|- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev2 (no P1; P2 F1/F2 production, P2 E1/E2 evidence, 7 P3; the rest — harness 70/70, 72/72 ratio, real-kill seam, hygiene — reproduced by the reviewer): F1 makes the same-key retry after `status` executable — a bound key without its completion reconciles through the production status entry, resumes under the same receipt when status proves the source (quiesce, stop-not-closed, create-absent: one effect set, one completion, one receipt), and refuses uncertain on target/contradiction/unknown; F2 fences the stale incarnation under a remote winner by asking the landed gate from the winner's own host (no local tuple comparison), from active/parked/quiescing, keeping the winning token as no-transition; E1 pins the create row's entry auth/generation/headless gates (no receipt bound) plus the committed second-effect timeout; E2 rotates lease+generation before the third stop effect and drifts the reported session on both status paths plus all five other axes both ways; P3-1 restores the source on pre-link store failure (post-link/lookup failures fence uncertain); P3-2 bounds fencing sources to the live states; P3-3 pins the deadline instant on both entries; P3-4 adds attach/none to the kind negatives; P3-6 replaces the kind twin with a landed `TransitionAuthorization` accessor (registered in the backend's census/inventory/audit batteries); P3-7 and `holder_host_id`-unbound recorded as stated leaf contracts.\n57|- REVERSAL (F2 of the rev2 entry, stated explicitly): \"pending-without-done is the honest interrupted state and its retry refuses `terminal_backend_unavailable`\" is FALSE as of rev3 for the proven-source case — the retry now reconciles through status and resumes under the same receipt when status proves the source, refusing uncertain only while the observation is genuinely unknown (target/contradiction/read-failure). TRACEABILITY rows 70/71 reworded to the resumed behavior; the `StoreHooks` doc sentence now states reconcile-instead-of-replay.\n58|- F1: an uncertain retry must reconcile through the production status entry rather than accept a caller-supplied report — a cached proof would let a stale source authorize a re-issue, while the engine's own exact-instance read cannot go stale; the query binds all six identity axes so a lying backend cannot authorize a resumption, and re-issue under the same key relies on the backend's own key binding (§13.13 safe_retry: never a second key, never a second process).\n59|- F2: the landed gate's arm order (\"the operative fact beats the credential\") hides staleness under a remote winner behind `remote_owner`, so the projection must ask twice — once as the local host, once relative to the winner — and fence only when the relative verdict is stale; both questions stay inside `fencing.Authorize`, which is composition, not a second model.\n60|- F3: the resumption's `err != nil` and `report.State != source` checks are one behavioral arm in two adjacent checks (status returns the empty report on every error path), so its narrowing row spans both and admits exactly the timeout-coded failed read; either half patched alone is masked by the other.\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
