{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c773","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c36e-d989-7603-9e05-f0fee9b1e516"},"sequence":532,"recorded_at":1780531400001059,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c371-06b5-7f12-89c8-00b7a77956a0"},"task_id":"01a0c371-06b5-7f12-89c8-00b7a77956a0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c371-06b5-7f12-89c8-00b7a77956a0","chunk":"Read text file `internal/axpane/run.go`.\n1|package axpane\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"errors\"\n5|\t\"fmt\"\n6|\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/config\"\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/fencing\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n11|)\n12|\n13|// Request is the complete Run surface: the session and bootstrap\n14|// operation under decision plus every modeled-caller fact the\n15|// adapters cannot load from the durable stores (sync state,\n16|// provider build and identity, backend documents, realm readiness,\n17|// presentation geometry). The stores supply configuration,\n18|// sessions, leases, journals, checkpoints, and bindings.\n19|type Request struct {\n20|\tSessionID            string\n21|\tBootstrapOperationID string\n22|\tMode                 Mode\n23|\n24|\tConfigInputs    config.Inputs\n25|\tConfigOverrides config.Overrides\n26|\n27|\t// Presented is the local fencing token; Observe carries the\n28|\t// caller-reported sync, handoff, grant, and clock facts.\n29|\tPresented fencing.PresentedToken\n30|\tObserve   fencing.ObserveInput\n31|\n32|\t// Materialization selects the required journal: when Required\n33|\t// is set the adapter loads ID and the decision requires the\n34|\t// committed phase (after-restore step 3).\n35|\tMaterializationID       string\n36|\tMaterializationRequired bool\n37|\n38|\t// Checkpoint selects the resume checkpoint: when Required is\n39|\t// set the adapter loads ID and the decision admits it.\n40|\tCheckpointID       string\n41|\tCheckpointRequired bool\n42|\n43|\tProvider ProviderFacts\n44|\tSmoke    SmokeFacts\n45|\tRealm    Realm\n46|\tBackend  BackendFacts\n47|\n48|\t// Entrypoint is the wrapper argv.\n49|\tEntrypoint []string\n50|\n51|\t// HostBinding is the AX-validated host-local binding subset\n52|\t// the supplied descriptor must match. Geometry and\n53|\t// interactivity shape the supplied descriptor; InstanceID\n54|\t// pins the terminal instance, or mints a fresh UUIDv7 when\n55|\t// empty.\n56|\tHostBinding terminalbackend.InstanceBinding\n57|\tInteractive bool\n58|\tColumns     uint16\n59|\tRows        uint16\n60|\tInstanceID  string\n61|\n62|\t// RemoteInteractive reports that the remote owner holds the\n63|\t// session in an interactive terminal (after-restore step 4).\n64|\tRemoteInteractive bool\n65|\n66|\t// LocalHostID authors parked events; CreatedAt stamps them.\n67|\tLocalHostID string\n68|\tCreatedAt   string\n69|\n70|\t// Hooks arms the bootstrap binding crash boundaries.\n71|\tHooks *Hooks\n72|}\n73|\n74|// Outcome is the one Run result: the decision plus the durable\n75|// effects it authorized. Exactly one effect applies: a launch binds\n76|// the bootstrap pair (superseding after the window closed), a\n77|// reattach returns the recorded binding, a parked or remote-offer\n78|// decision with a locally held, verified winner and a foldable\n79|// lifecycle authors the parked event, and every other outcome\n80|// writes nothing.\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
