{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c915","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c36e-d989-7603-9e05-f0fee9b1e516"},"sequence":741,"recorded_at":1780531400001477,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623"},"call_id":"call_01a0c371a2d3738ea8f574e28104a5e4","text":"Read text file `internal/environ/doc.go`.\n1|// Package environ is the single environment library behind the\n2|// Provider, Session Adapter, and Directory Node facades.\n3|//\n4|// Pinned specification v0.5.0 requires the Directory Node facade to\n5|// expose source-local environment discovery \"through the same\n6|// parsers, identity logic, redaction rules, tuple gates, and\n7|// fixtures as the Provider and Session Adapter facades\" (Section\n8|// 3.1), backed by \"the same environment implementation as Provider\n9|// 2 and Session Adapter 1\" (Sections 7.9, 10.8, 13.14). Before this\n10|// package each facade carried its own copy of those rules, and\n11|// independent copies of the same rule drift in ways no per-facade\n12|// reviewer can see. This package is the one implementation every\n13|// facade must converge on:\n14|//\n15|//   - frame parsing: DecodeStrictObject is the only JSON entry\n16|//     point, with duplicate-member rejection and the Section 1.6\n17|//     lone-surrogate gate in canonical string-walk semantics;\n18|//   - string measure: CheckStringBounds counts Unicode characters\n19|//     (runes), never bytes and never UTF-16 code units;\n20|//   - shared grammars: the environment-id, provider-id (via\n21|//     scalar), SemVer, platform, and architecture rules;\n22|//   - tuple gates: DecodeTuple admits the exact six-member\n23|//     Environment Tuple of Sections 7.8 and 13.14, which never\n24|//     carries executable provenance or extensions;\n25|//   - observation gates: DecodeEnvironmentObservation admits the\n26|//     Section 10.8.1 Environment Observation, reusing the tuple\n27|//     admission model rather than creating a second one.\n28|//\n29|// Every refusal is a plain error whose text names the rule and the\n30|// member: facades keep their own refusal dialects (Structured\n31|// Error codes per protocol), so this package names rules instead\n32|// of minting codes, and the boundary battery pins each facade's\n33|// rendering separately.\n34|//\n35|// Stated bounds. Provider Identity refusal dialects stay in\n36|// provhost and canonicaljson: the two validators must agree\n37|// rule-for-rule and the agreement battery in this package pins\n38|// that, but a third validator here would be another copy, not\n39|// convergence. Byte-counted exec rules (Provider SpawnPlan argv\n40|// and env literals, Section 5.1) stay in provhost: they bound\n41|// bytes by specification while every character-bound member in\n42|// this story counts runes, and the measure battery ledgers that\n43|// split. The tuple-registry signature, sequence monotonicity, and\n44|// publication rules of Section 13.14 fail closed at the registry\n45|// owner, which does not exist yet. This package mutates no durable\n46|// state and keeps no cache: every entry point is a pure function\n47|// of its input bytes.\n48|package environ","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c917","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c36e-d989-7603-9e05-f0fee9b1e516"},"sequence":742,"recorded_at":1780531400001479,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623"},"call_id":"call_01a0c371a5d57099b3a742a8329751b7","text":"Read text file `internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py`.\n1|#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2|\"\"\"Narrowing-mutant harness for internal/termbind.\n3|\n4|Every gate ships a narrowing mutant: the gate stays present and is\n5|weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and\n6|the named killer tests must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that\n7|the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence; row D-emit-noresolve is\n8|the one explicitly supplementary arm-delete (the producer-named drop),\n9|labeled as such and not counted as any gate's narrowing.\n10|\n11|Each row runs M (mutate production files in place), R (run the scoped Go\n12|killers through the production entries), V (verdict from the Go exit code\n13|plus a FAIL kill-line: KILLED iff R fails with a test failure line,\n14|SURVIVED iff R passes, ERROR for anything else -- unapplied patches,\n15|build breaks, timeouts). M failures and R infrastructure errors are\n16|ERROR, never kills or survivals. Files are restored from backups after\n17|every row, pass or fail.\n18|\n19|Row C-control is the harmless control: a comment-only edit that must\n20|SURVIVE, proving the harness observes test outcomes instead of\n21|hard-coding kills.\n22|\n23|Two plants are honestly not rows: attach cannot emit an event because\n24|Attach takes no repository (absence by construction, proven by\n25|TestAttachEmitsNeitherEventNorStateChange -- no text plant can add a\n26|write), and the lease-authority narrowing belongs to the adopted axpane\n27|rows N-emit-mutation and N-emit-losing-epoch (composition pinned here by\n28|TestEmitUnderLosingLeaseRefuses).\n29|\n30|Usage:\n31|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py\n32|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py N-identity-pid\n33|  AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1 PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py N-identity-pid\n34|\"\"\"\n35|\n36|import os\n37|import shutil\n38|import subprocess\n39|import sys\n40|import tempfile\n41|from dataclasses import dataclass\n42|from pathlib import Path\n43|\n44|REPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n45|PACKAGE = \"internal/termbind\"\n46|\n47|DD_DIGEST = \"sha256:\" + \"dd\" * 32\n48|OTHER_OP = \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ac\"\n49|\n50|\n51|@dataclass(frozen=True)\n52|class Mutant:\n53|    name: str\n54|    path: str\n55|    find: str\n56|    replace: str\n57|    count: int\n58|    run: str\n59|    expect: str\n60|    note: str\n61|    find2: str = \"\"\n62|    replace2: str = \"\"\n63|    count2: int = 0\n64|\n65|\n66|IDENTITY_KILLERS = (\n67|    \"(TestCheckInstanceIdentityRefusesForbiddenForms\"\n68|    \"|TestParseTerminalBindingRefusesForbiddenIdentity\"\n69|    \"|TestAdmitMutationContextRefusesForbiddenIdentity\"\n70|    \"|TestAdmitStatusBodyRefusesForbiddenIdentity\"\n71|    \"|TestAttachRefusesForbiddenIdentity)\"\n72|)\n73|\n74|MUTANTS = [\n75|    Mutant(\n76|        name=\"N-identity-pid\",\n77|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n78|        find='\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(value); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn &terminalbackend.Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"terminal instance identity\"}\\n\\t}\\n',\n79|        replace='\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(value); err != nil && value != \"12345\" {\\n\\t\\treturn &terminalbackend.Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"terminal instance identity\"}\\n\\t}\\n',\n80|        count=1,\n81|        run=IDENTITY_KILLERS,\n82|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n83|        note=\"Admits exactly the PID form at the shared identity gate; every other forbidden form still refuses on all five surfaces.\",\n84|    ),\n85|    Mutant(\n86|        name=\"N-identity-endpoint\",\n87|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n88|        find='\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(value); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn &terminalbackend.Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"terminal instance identity\"}\\n\\t}\\n',\n89|        replace='\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(value); err != nil && value != \"10.0.0.9:2222\" {\\n\\t\\treturn &terminalbackend.Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"terminal instance identity\"}\\n\\t}\\n',\n90|        count=1,\n91|        run=IDENTITY_KILLERS,\n92|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n93|        note=\"Admits exactly the endpoint form at the shared identity gate; every other forbidden form still refuses on all five surfaces.\",\n94|    ),\n95|    Mutant(\n96|        name=\"N-binding-members\",\n97|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n98|        find=\"\\tif len(members) != len(bindingMembers) {\\n\",\n99|        replace=\"\\tif len(members) != len(bindingMembers) && len(members) != len(bindingMembers)+1 {\\n\",\n100|        count=1,\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
