{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c9b5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c36e-d989-7603-9e05-f0fee9b1e516"},"sequence":821,"recorded_at":1780531400001637,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c372-67e0-72c2-b97b-21fa876c6e23"},"task_id":"01a0c372-67e0-72c2-b97b-21fa876c6e23","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c372-67e0-72c2-b97b-21fa876c6e23","chunk":"Read text file `internal/secprim/open_member_unix.go`.\n1|//go:build !windows\n2|\n3|package secprim\n4|\n5|import (\n6|\t\"errors\"\n7|\t\"os\"\n8|\n9|\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n10|)\n11|\n12|// openCommitRelative walks one validated member from the staging-root\n13|// directory handle to an open file descriptor without ever re-resolving\n14|// a path string: every component is opened relative to the previous\n15|// component's descriptor with openat. Intermediate components carry\n16|// O_NOFOLLOW|O_DIRECTORY, so a symlinked directory on the path fails\n17|// with ELOOP instead of redirecting the walk outside the root; the\n18|// final component carries O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK, so a trailing symlink\n19|// fails with ELOOP and a FIFO returns immediately instead of stalling\n20|// the opener until a writer appears. Descriptors pin what they opened:\n21|// a rename or swap after any step cannot retarget a descriptor the\n22|// walk already holds, which is what closes the validate-then-open\n23|// TOCTOU rather than repeating it with more steps.\n24|//\n25|// The walk reports no refusal of its own: ELOOP maps to the shared\n26|// errCommitSymlink signal (refused as \"member symlink escape\" by the\n27|// caller) and every other failure returns raw (refused as \"open\n28|// failed\" with its cause). Shape checks on the final descriptor stay\n29|// with the caller, which stats the descriptor rather than the path.\n30|//\n31|// rootPath is the guard root the caller already bound to root with\n32|// guardRootMatches before descending: the walk descends from the\n33|// handle alone because descriptors pin what they opened, while the\n34|// Windows walk descends from the verified path string. Both name the\n35|// same directory past the shared binding check, so the containment\n36|// root is one value on both platforms, not one per walk.\n37|//\n38|// Error classification runs before any descriptor is closed: from the\n39|// second intermediate onward previous == current, so closing first\n40|// would fstat a recycled descriptor number and misreport the shape.\n41|func openCommitRelative(root *os.File, rootPath string, member string, segments []string) (*os.File, error) {\n42|\t// rootPath names the guard root already bound to root by the\n43|\t// caller; it is documentation here, enforcement in Guard.Open.\n44|\t_ = rootPath\n45|\tprevious := -1\n46|\tcurrent := int(root.Fd())\n47|\tfor _, segment := range segments[:len(segments)-1] {\n48|\t\tnext, err := unix.Openat(current, segment,\n49|\t\t\tunix.O_RDONLY|unix.O_NOFOLLOW|unix.O_DIRECTORY|unix.O_CLOEXEC, 0)\n50|\t\tif err != nil {\n51|\t\t\tclassified := classifyCommitErr(current, segment, err)\n52|\t\t\tif previous >= 0 {\n53|\t\t\t\t_ = unix.Close(previous)\n54|\t\t\t}\n55|\t\t\treturn nil, classified\n56|\t\t}\n57|\t\tif previous >= 0 {\n58|\t\t\t_ = unix.Close(previous)\n59|\t\t}\n60|\t\tprevious, current = next, next\n61|\t}\n62|\tlast := segments[len(segments)-1]\n63|\tfinal, err := unix.Openat(current, last,\n64|\t\tunix.O_RDONLY|unix.O_NOFOLLOW|unix.O_CLOEXEC|unix.O_NONBLOCK, 0)\n65|\tif err != nil {\n66|\t\tclassified := classifyCommitErr(current, last, err)\n67|\t\tif previous >= 0 {\n68|\t\t\t_ = unix.Close(previous)\n69|\t\t}\n70|\t\treturn nil, classified\n71|\t}\n72|\tif previous >= 0 {\n73|\t\t_ = unix.Close(previous)\n74|\t}\n75|\treturn os.NewFile(uintptr(final), member), nil\n76|}\n77|\n78|// classifyCommitErr sorts the walk failures: a symlink anywhere on the\n79|// path becomes the escape signal, while a missing component, a file\n80|// where a directory stands, or a permission failure stays raw for the\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
