{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d4ef","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c36e-d989-7603-9e05-f0fee9b1e516"},"sequence":2258,"recorded_at":1780531400004511,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c384-11b4-7bf1-9b8d-55f8a613ec1e"},"task_id":"01a0c384-11b4-7bf1-9b8d-55f8a613ec1e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c384-11b4-7bf1-9b8d-55f8a613ec1e","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 2320-2329\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-The harness mutates one production file in place, runs the named killer\n-through the production entry point, restores the file from backup, and\n-reports per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1`\n-additionally prints the raw per-plant logs. Task validation logs and\n-mutation artifacts are attached to `TASK-260830-2056mm`. The package\n-adds no `ax` command, no `doctor` result, and no runtime capability\n-claim; the clause-to-test matrix with its stated bounds lives in\n-[the task evidence map](internal/termbind/TRACEABILITY.md).\n-\n-## Ownership reducer properties\n+The harness mutates one production file in place, runs the named killer\n+through the production entry point, restores the file from backup, and\n+reports per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1`\n+additionally prints the raw per-plant logs. Task validation logs and\n+mutation artifacts are attached to `TASK-260830-2056mm`. The package\n+adds no `ax` command, no `doctor` result, and no runtime capability\n+claim; the clause-to-test matrix with its stated bounds lives in\n+[the task evidence map](internal/termbind/TRACEABILITY.md).\n+\n+## Private tmux server management (`tmuxserver` leaf)\n+\n+[`internal/tmuxserver`](internal/tmuxserver) creates owner-only runtime\n+directories and manages dedicated `tmux -S` servers with no ambient or\n+default-server discovery or reuse (pinned Sections 4.2, 4.C-4.E).\n+`EnsureRuntimeDir` commits the runtime leaf relative to a pinned root\n+handle (`mkdirat`, never a path-string `MkdirAll`) and enforces three\n+independent custody gates — containment, exact `0700` mode, effective-UID\n+ownership — each of which refuses alone; an existing directory is\n+verified, never silently repaired. `ResolveSocket` derives the one\n+server socket from the runtime directory and refuses any explicit\n+override, whether it arrives as a `TMUX` environment value, an inherited\n+socket, a default path, or the conventional `default` name. `Acquire`\n+reaches the server through the caller-appropriate path: foreground\n+attaches to the running attested server or spawns the dedicated `-S`\n+server whose stable pane entrypoint is `ax pane SESSION_ID`, while\n+background contacts only the already-running authenticated broker and\n+its attested server, and otherwise returns the typed\n+`capability_unavailable` refusal with realm/readiness details — there is\n+no fallback to direct creation, and every background test arms a spy\n+spawner that fails the run if it is ever invoked. `CheckLiveAttestation`\n+admits only a complete live observation (passed sentinel and\n+provider-auth smoke bound to the exact server generation, provider\n+build, and macOS version); the `launchctl managername` hint and any\n+cached sentinel observation travel for diagnostics only and authorize\n+nothing. Every broker, server, and spawner interaction runs through\n+injected dependencies, so the suite passes with no tmux process\n+anywhere.\n+\n+Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n+\n+```bash\n+go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\n+go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\n+```\n+\n+Run the narrowing battery (29 narrowing mutants, one supplementary\n+additive row, plus one harmless control) with:\n+\n+```bash\n+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py\n+```\n+\n+The harness mutates one production file in place, runs the named killer\n+through the production entry point, restores the file from backup, and\n+reports per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1`\n+additionally prints the raw per-plant logs, and `--log-dir` captures one\n+raw log per plant. Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are\n+attached to `TASK-260830-35urbp`. The package adds no `ax` command, no\n+`doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim; the clause-to-test\n+matrix with its stated bounds lives in\n+[the task evidence map](internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md).\n+\n+## Ownership reducer properties\n","final_result":true}}}
