{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d523","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c36e-d989-7603-9e05-f0fee9b1e516"},"sequence":2284,"recorded_at":1780531400004563,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c384-4980-7933-8851-09217b380d62"},"task_id":"01a0c384-4980-7933-8851-09217b380d62","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c384-4980-7933-8851-09217b380d62","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-6\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-# Flight Logbook\n-\n-> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n-> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n-\n-## 2026-09-18\n+# Flight Logbook\n+\n+> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n+> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n+\n+## 2026-09-21\n+\n+### TASK-260830-35urbp — Private tmux server management (first leaf, STORY-260830-2t4g7i)\n+\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/tmuxserver` — the §4.2/§4.C-4.E first leaf over the landed owners: `EnsureRuntimeDir` commits the runtime leaf via `mkdirat` from a pinned root handle with three independent custody gates (containment, exact `0700`, eUID ownership, each refusing alone; existing dirs verified, never repaired); `ResolveSocket` derives the one `-S` socket from the runtime dir and refuses any override on all four ambient vectors (TMUX env, inherited socket, default path, conventional name); `Acquire` attaches/spawns on foreground and brokers-or-refuses on background with the typed `capability_unavailable` (via `axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable`) and no fallback — the miss path consults the creation gate by call, and every background test arms a zero-call spy spawner; `CheckLiveAttestation` admits only complete live sentinel+smoke bound to generation/build/macOS, while the managername hint and cached observations travel diagnostics-only and authorize nothing; `BuildArgv` emits the exact `tmux -S socket new-session -d -s session ax pane session` vector through the landed argv gate. No test starts tmux: all probes/spawns are injected fakes.\n+- F1: a structural absence (\"this path has no spawn call\") is not an enforceable gate until a call exists to weaken — the background miss path now consults `checkCreationAllowed` by call so the N-creation-literal narrowing (background admitted) reddens through the entry with the creation code instead of the typed unavailable, and the D-background-fallback additive plant (reviewer-shaped direct-creation call) reddens on the spy assertions.\n+- F2: `Fchmod` before verification silently repairs — the create path now chmods only leaves it created (`Mkdirat` success, for umask) while pre-existing leaves verify as-is, so a widened `0755` refuses on both ensure and verify instead of being narrowed back.\n+- F3: single-member refusal classes still narrow honestly — `caller == \"background\"` weakens to the capitalized twin (gate present, one member admitted), and delegated wirings (scalar UUIDv7/platform/path grammars) narrow at our call site with reroute kills, never by re-testing the owner.\n+- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 29 narrowing mutants plus one supplementary additive row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 31/31 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical. No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text. Suite: 89 subtests green, 87.5% statement coverage; `GOOS=windows` builds.\n+- AC: 54 of 54 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence via real SIGKILL between mkdir and fsync plus spawn-then-retry convergence. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n+- BOUNDS: no real-tmux witness for any row (determinism design); Windows ownership is the creating-user ACL (tripwire-pinned); attach presentation vectors and lifecycle operations are sibling-leaf scope; registry bindings and the digest re-pin belong to the final leaf.\n+\n+## 2026-09-18\n","final_result":true}}}
