{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d5eb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c36e-d989-7603-9e05-f0fee9b1e516"},"sequence":2384,"recorded_at":1780531400004763,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c389-e6b4-7b10-89b5-374e3dde77fc"},"task_id":"01a0c389-e6b4-7b10-89b5-374e3dde77fc","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c389-e6b4-7b10-89b5-374e3dde77fc","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-39-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board q 'get(TASK-260830-35urbp) { checklist notes }' 2>&1 | head -n 60\\necho \\\"===\\\"\\ntask-board resource --help 2>&1 | head -n 30\",\n  \"description\": \"Check checklist and resource upload\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"checklist\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Create owner-only runtime directories and dedicated tmux -S servers without ambient/default discovery or reuse\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft \\\\u003ccheckpoint_oid\\\\u003e` before completing again.\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Lint clean\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\",\\\"done\\\":false}],\\\"notes\\\":\\\"spawn workload selection: class=implementation source=explicit policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=muse/muse-spark/max pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:009eecf230ad676c71fa02f210ad171dc6936cae601b3bc028fa753d219ff3c1 rationale=\\\\\\\"First leaf of STORY-260830-2t4g7i (production tmux backend): dedicated -S server management with owner-only runtime directories, the background-caller credential refusal and a hard determinism constraint. muse-spark max is rank 1 for implementation in the fresh snapshot and is the operator's producer routing for this epic.\\\\\\\"\\\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: muse via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[muse,codex,claude], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260921-e93883, max_parallel=20)\\\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260921-e93883)\\\"}\\n===\\nManage attached resources such as screenshots, docs, logs, and other files.\\n\\nUse \\\"task-board resource add\\\" to create a new attached resource, \\\"task-board\\nresource adopt\\\" to register an orphaned local payload, \\\"task-board resource\\nupdate\\\" to replace an existing one, \\\"task-board resource delete\\\" to remove it,\\nand \\\"task-board resource get\\\" to materialize a resource back to the local\\nfilesystem for inspection.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  task-board resource [command]\\n\\nAvailable Commands:\\n  add         Attach a new file resource to an element\\n  adopt       Register an existing unreferenced local resource payload\\n  delete      Delete a resource from an element (requires --confirm)\\n  get         Download a resource to the local filesystem\\n  update      Replace an existing file resource on an element\\n\\nFlags:\\n  -h, --help   help for resource\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --board-dir string         Path to the board directory (overrides TASK_BOARD_DIR and config local.board_dir) (default \\\".task-board\\\")\\n      --context-profile string   Agent context profile override: full or lite\\n      --insecure                 Skip TLS certificate verification (for self-signed certs)\\n      --json                     Output in JSON format\\n      --no-update-check          Disable automatic update check\\n      --remote string            Remote board server URL (overrides TASK_BOARD_REMOTE)\\n      --remote-board string      Remote board ID (overrides TASK_BOARD_ID)\\n\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4822,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1206,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
