{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d91b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c36e-d989-7603-9e05-f0fee9b1e516"},"sequence":2792,"recorded_at":1780531400005579,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"78e4a4f8-26f7-4967-82c0-c54272cc4623"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review.\n\nTASK-260830-35urbp is `to-review` (checklist 14/14, three task-scoped outcomes attached). The candidate is the uncommitted working tree on `task-board/story/STORY-260830-2t4g7i`: new [internal/tmuxserver](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-2t4g7i/worktree/internal/tmuxserver/doc.go) plus a README package section and one LOGBOOK entry. No commit was made; branch tip is still `799c338`.\n\nWhat was delivered:\n\n- `EnsureRuntimeDir`/`VerifyRuntimeDir` — owner-only runtime dir via `mkdirat` from a pinned handle, with three independent gates (containment, exact `0700`, eUID ownership) that each refuse alone; existing dirs verify, never repair.\n- `ResolveSocket` — the one `-S` socket derived from the runtime dir; overrides refuse on all four ambient vectors (TMUX env, inherited socket, default path, conventional name) plus collision.\n- `Acquire` — foreground attaches/spawns; background brokers-or-refuses with typed `capability_unavailable` (exit 6, all five details) and no fallback, enforced by a gate call with zero-call spy spawners on every background test.\n- `CheckLiveAttestation`/`CheckBrokerContact` — only complete live sentinel+smoke bound to generation/build/macOS admits; managername hint and cached observations are diagnostics-only.\n- `BuildArgv` — exact `tmux -S socket new-session -d -s session ax pane session` through the landed argv gate.\n\nEvidence (measured, all rerun in this session):\n\n- 54 of 54 AC rows driven through production entries by named tests; matrix in `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md` and the attached conformance matrix.\n- Mutant battery 31/31 on two passes with identical verdicts: 29 narrowing KILLED, 1 supplementary additive KILLED, 1 control SURVIVED, one raw log per plant per run, no `__pycache__`.\n- Crash/idempotency via real SIGKILL between mkdir and fsync plus spawn-then-retry convergence.\n- `go vet`, `gofmt`, `go test ./...` and `go test ./... -cover` all green (45/45, 0 FAIL); package coverage 87.5% (89 subtests); `GOOS=windows` builds.\n- No test starts tmux and no row has a real-tmux witness — the determinism design, stated as bound B1 with seven further bounds (B2–B8).\n\nTwo notes for the reviewer: the producer's \"30 configured commands\" does not exist in this worktree's `task-board.config.json` (no `validation.commands` section), so the AGENTS.md gates above are what ran; and `task-board validate` reports only pre-existing issues on other elements, none on this task.","reason":null}}
